# ═══ AN ALLOW LIST: BY DEFAULT NOTHING IS TAKEN ═════════════════════════════
#
# The operator's design (2026-08-29): a deny list errs towards ADMITTING — any
# kind of file nobody foresaw slips into history silently. An allow list errs
# towards REFUSING — a new kind of file stays out until someone decides it is
# the product, and that mistake shows at once and costs one line to fix.
#
# This is the PRODUCT's list. An installation's data — chats, settings, grants,
# rules, the token, logs, queues, the tamper watch's approved state — is never
# admitted here, whatever an installation's own git may choose to track. On
# 2026-09-10 a deny list had let a runtime log carrying live chat ids sit in this
# repository for nineteen days.
*
!*/
!*.py
!*.md
!*.example
!*.service
!LICENSE
!.gitignore
!locale/
!locale/*.json
# and still keep out what the admissions above would let slip through
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pyc
__pycache__/
